bcom:source-86ebec3b3a2fd6ef8f8882da534522db5a85e3ae1bcdffad76e3e6a5aa1a254c bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-86ebec3b3a2fd6ef8f8882da534522db5a85e3ae1bcdffad76e3e6a5aa1a254c bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-GOV-04 .
bcom:source-86ebec3b3a2fd6ef8f8882da534522db5a85e3ae1bcdffad76e3e6a5aa1a254c bco:departureNote "NAF defines a capability by what one or more resources can be expected to deliver, and its resources cover systems and equipment as well as organizations. The BCO narrows the bearer to an Organization (CD1); an organization-borne capability is a special case NAF permits, so the BCO narrows NAF rather than contradicting it."@en .
bcom:source-86ebec3b3a2fd6ef8f8882da534522db5a85e3ae1bcdffad76e3e6a5aa1a254c bco:locator "NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide, glossary, PDF p.154 (Capability)" .
bcom:source-86ebec3b3a2fd6ef8f8882da534522db5a85e3ae1bcdffad76e3e6a5aa1a254c bco:relation "departs-from" .

bcom:source-897542f462f9b69159da97b0bcd489ad4d9052dfdcb4ccd829c7802e71470932 bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-BA-08 .
bcom:source-897542f462f9b69159da97b0bcd489ad4d9052dfdcb4ccd829c7802e71470932 bco:locator "Offerman et al. 2017, p. 384 (the level sense of capability, kept apart from its availability)" .
bcom:source-897542f462f9b69159da97b0bcd489ad4d9052dfdcb4ccd829c7802e71470932 bco:relation "consistent-with" .
bcom:source-897542f462f9b69159da97b0bcd489ad4d9052dfdcb4ccd829c7802e71470932 bco:support "contextual" .

bcom:source-8ffd8e3467f36e58e1545a9560b3bcc718cedceab0f8acebfaf87e4394dbe9b6 bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-8ffd8e3467f36e58e1545a9560b3bcc718cedceab0f8acebfaf87e4394dbe9b6 bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-ISO-06 .
bcom:source-8ffd8e3467f36e58e1545a9560b3bcc718cedceab0f8acebfaf87e4394dbe9b6 bco:departureNote "Homonym. ISO/IEC 33020 process capability is a quality characteristic of a process, and its capability level is derived from process attribute ratings. A Capability Maturity Rating ranks an existing Organization Capability instance, never a process, and is not a process capability level (register SF-10)."@en .
bcom:source-8ffd8e3467f36e58e1545a9560b3bcc718cedceab0f8acebfaf87e4394dbe9b6 bco:locator "ISO catalogue page 78526, abstract of ISO/IEC 33020:2019" .
bcom:source-8ffd8e3467f36e58e1545a9560b3bcc718cedceab0f8acebfaf87e4394dbe9b6 bco:relation "departs-from" .

bcom:source-9019f46e59d576e4f705ea1fa96b722f01f5b871137033fa57cfa273fc1d8d2c bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-9019f46e59d576e4f705ea1fa96b722f01f5b871137033fa57cfa273fc1d8d2c bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-GOV-04 .
bcom:source-9019f46e59d576e4f705ea1fa96b722f01f5b871137033fa57cfa273fc1d8d2c bco:departureNote "NAF's Capability Configuration, the nearest analogue of a material basis, combines people and technology. The BCO's material basis is the organization's member agents only (CD2); systems, equipment and facilities are enabling conditions that take part in realizations, and losing one makes the capability unavailable, not absent."@en .
bcom:source-9019f46e59d576e4f705ea1fa96b722f01f5b871137033fa57cfa273fc1d8d2c bco:locator "NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide, glossary, PDF p.154 (Capability Configuration)" .
bcom:source-9019f46e59d576e4f705ea1fa96b722f01f5b871137033fa57cfa273fc1d8d2c bco:relation "departs-from" .

bcom:source-9696a1e1c45bfa5af948ea71d53d815a3b20d13c4aca063cd4b0516dff8b3159 bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-BA-08 .
bcom:source-9696a1e1c45bfa5af948ea71d53d815a3b20d13c4aca063cd4b0516dff8b3159 bco:locator "Offerman et al. 2017, p. 384 (the senses of capability split into its level and its availability)" .
bcom:source-9696a1e1c45bfa5af948ea71d53d815a3b20d13c4aca063cd4b0516dff8b3159 bco:relation "consistent-with" .
bcom:source-9696a1e1c45bfa5af948ea71d53d815a3b20d13c4aca063cd4b0516dff8b3159 bco:support "contextual" .

bcom:source-97e23ec03caae84d0e2db9e06c148b5089b25a70bc274c4547be16bdbd40bbdf bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-97e23ec03caae84d0e2db9e06c148b5089b25a70bc274c4547be16bdbd40bbdf bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-OMG-04 .
bcom:source-97e23ec03caae84d0e2db9e06c148b5089b25a70bc274c4547be16bdbd40bbdf bco:departureNote "UAF lets any CapableElement (operational agent, service, actual resource or actual organization) exhibit a capability. A Business Capability inheres in an Organization and in nothing else (CD1); abilities of persons, systems and other resources are not Business Capabilities."@en .
bcom:source-97e23ec03caae84d0e2db9e06c148b5089b25a70bc274c4547be16bdbd40bbdf bco:locator "UAF 1.3 DMM, Traceability package: CapableElement and the Exhibits relation (the omg-and-iso note records no page for these)" .
bcom:source-97e23ec03caae84d0e2db9e06c148b5089b25a70bc274c4547be16bdbd40bbdf bco:relation "departs-from" .

bcom:source-9e0ae7b454e724daac1ace5bb02dd6384fb5f28e00f986bd1102b13207d5cd9e bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-9e0ae7b454e724daac1ace5bb02dd6384fb5f28e00f986bd1102b13207d5cd9e bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-FO-12 .
bcom:source-9e0ae7b454e724daac1ace5bb02dd6384fb5f28e00f986bd1102b13207d5cd9e bco:departureNote "In CDD the Capability doubles as the requirement for an ability to meet a goal. The BCO keeps the two apart: the requirement is a Capability Target, an Objective that prescribes that an organization come to bear a capability of a given type, and the capability itself is a disposition the target does not imply exists."@en .
bcom:source-9e0ae7b454e724daac1ace5bb02dd6384fb5f28e00f986bd1102b13207d5cd9e bco:locator "CaaS project, Definitions of concepts web page (Capability is required by a Goal and serves to formulate requirements)" .
